## 2.1 Initial business

Business name: Saber Dates

Initial product:

- Product: Piarom Dates
- Packaging: Transparent plastic package
- Net weight: 600 grams
- Initial demonstration inventory: 200 packages
- Initial currency: Iranian Toman
- Interface language: Persian
- Interface direction: RTL

The product brand name, logo, descriptions, product photographs, and business information must be editable from the administrator dashboard.

Do not hardcode the business identity into the application.

## 2.2 Future product expansion

The platform must support multiple products from the beginning.

The owner may later add:

- Mazafati Dates
- Kabkab Dates
- Other agricultural products
- Food products
- Non-agricultural products

Adding products must not require any source-code modifications.

All inventory, pricing, commissions, reports, and sales documents must support multiple products.

## 2.3 Two principal sales channels

### Channel A — B2B grocery store distribution

Products are delivered to grocery stores under a consignment arrangement.

The business initially does not collect payment when delivering products.

The grocery store sells products to its customers and reports the quantities sold.

The store pays the business according to the agreed settlement terms.

The business owner receives the amount corresponding to the products sold, while the retailer retains the agreed markup.

### Channel B — B2C direct consumer sales

Customers scan QR codes on product packages or visit the public website.

They can purchase products directly.

Payment must be completed before fulfillment.

The products are then prepared and delivered to the customer.

These channels must share product information and inventory infrastructure but have separate payment and settlement workflows.

